WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:01.199
Wow.

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.430
What an amazing way to end the season of The
Last of Us.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.380
Having played the game I knew this ending
would absolutely obliterate everyone and I

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.860
think the execution of the climax worked out
perfectly.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.560
Joel’s rampage through the hospital to save
Ellie while simultaneously dooming the world

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.550
is narrative brilliance.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.529
This story beat is amazing and Neil Druckman
for actually making this scenario believable

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:24.349
is astounding.

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:28.380
Because the fact that we actually kind of
sympathize with Joel here is a really hard

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.859
thing to do from a story perspective.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:33.450
Given that he murdered dozens of fireflies.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.570
Through the course of the show we’ve really
bonded to Joel and Ellie and the entire experiment

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.399
of this arc is if we’d accept what Joel
does here.

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:45.020
In order for us to accept this, we need to
fully understand the character and to be able

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.770
to relate to him.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:51.039
Having the sound slowly fade out and primarily
drive the emotion of Joel’s headspace with

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:54.940
music was an outstanding idea that helped
with this notion.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.600
It really submerges you into Joel’s twisted
and motivated perspective.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.880
What Joel is doing here is obviously not right,
but what makes this so compelling is that

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:07.440
he’s a character who’s solely motivated
by what he cares about the most.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.460
He’s someone who has been broken since the
death of Sarah and Ellie is what fixed him.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.570
This idea is expressed in probably one of
my favorite lines in a script in a while where

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:21.590
Joel and Ellie say this: “So time heals
all wounds, I guess.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:25.360
It wasn’t time that did it.”

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.030
What a smart way to communicate this without
saying it outright.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:33.930
Having Joel look at Ellie in this moment visually
says that she is the one that cured his depression

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.960
and her realizing that is peak writing to
me.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.649
And the crazy thing is that I think this is
a show-specific moment.

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:45.299
From how integral this line is for Joel’s
entire arc, I’m surprised it didn’t originate

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:46.299
in the game.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:49.810
Unless if they did say it at some point, but
it wasn’t in a cinematic.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:54.219
So this moment punctuates Joel’s arc perfectly
and I think is the best way to prepare the

00:01:54.219 --> 00:01:56.759
audience for the upcoming massacre.

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:01.111
In comparison to the game, I think people
were more motivated to save Ellie and to kill

00:02:01.111 --> 00:02:05.009
all of these people because of how much they’ve
already killed in the game.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:09.349
It kind of becomes additional violence and
the people you kill here blend into the already

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:11.860
big body count you’ve been accumulating.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.550
For the show, this is almost the opposite
because Joel and Ellie haven’t had to kill

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.780
as many people.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.420
So Joel making the decision to kill the fireflies
is even bigger here.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:23.980
It has more dramatic weight because we haven’t
been mowing people down.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:29.360
In both the game and the show they are definitely
impactful segments, but I think the show executes

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.720
it really well along with having a lot of
great moments to communicate how far gone

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.890
Joel is.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:39.030
Like him gunning down the unarmed firefly
and him having to finish off someone with

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.030
the knife.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:43.670
This particular moment feels like a mirror
to episode 4 where this drawn-out segment

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.720
of the guy’s death was really haunting and
difficult.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.040
The fact that Joel is unmoved by having to
execute this person and does it without hesitation

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.430
is a staggering contrast.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:03:00.150
And even the brief shot of showing Joel’s
face after killing the doctor is kind of terrifying.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.390
Joel becomes a monster here and it’s OK
to disagree with what he is doing.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.760
The show sets up both sides of the coin as
being immoral because even Marlene is killing

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.340
Ellie without her approval.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.400
Obviously, the correct thing to do is to ask
Ellie if she is willing to sacrifice herself

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.880
for the vaccine, but Marlene is equally doing
a bad thing by not giving her that choice.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.250
Which this is met by Joel’s outrage.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:26.920
So from a character point of view, everyone
here makes sense and it all clashes with one

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.670
of the best climaxes in video game and even
show history.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.950
From here on out it basically follows the
game exactly which makes sense because I think

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.780
the ending is spectacular.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:41.459
Through Ellie questioning Joel and the circumstances
in which they left, she knows that he is probably

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:42.760
lying to her.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:47.200
So her giving him one final chance to come
clean at the end and puts their entire trust

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.810
on the line I think speaks volumes for what
she knows deep down.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:55.099
So having Joel double down on the lie and
compromise their trust is a tragic ending

00:03:55.099 --> 00:04:00.270
despite it supposedly being uplifting since
Joel and Ellie are back together again.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:03.909
From here, the question remains as to how
this will impact their relationship going

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:08.310
forward and will Ellie ever find out the truth
of what really happened.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.069
So the ending was executed to a complete tee
in comparison to the game and retained that

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:14.550
gut-punch of an ending.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:18.549
I’m happy nothing was changed and despite
people saying that the ending was originally

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:22.600
controversial, I think it has always been
an outstanding ending.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.990
From here let's go into some of the other
strengths of the episode.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.140
In particular, I loved the cold opening.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:32.590
I kind of missed this tradition that was set
up by the first two episodes and I’m glad

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:36.900
it returned because it has the opportunity
to flesh out the world a lot more.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.050
Having the actress who played Ellie in the
game play her mother is such a genius way

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.240
to pass on the torch and quite literally at
that.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.550
But the fact that this scene offers way more
than just seeing Ellie’s origin is great.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.580
We simultaneously learn how Ellie gained her
immunity through her mom getting bit before

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.830
she cut the umbilical cord and seeing Marlene’s
relationship with Ellie’s mother.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:01.120
In the game, Marlene’s connection to Ellie
was pretty underdeveloped because her only

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.900
scene was her giving Ellie to Joel and Tess.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.920
Along with the ending.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:09.310
For the show, they develop her character a
lot more which was a good change because it

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:12.250
makes her eventual demise that much more moving.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.520
We understand the hurt and conflict within
her to kill Ellie for the greater good and

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.380
it offers an interesting contrast between
her and Joel.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.650
They both care for Ellie but since Joel has
been shattered by Sarah, it’s impossible

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.720
for him to give her up without fighting.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.020
While Marlene is on the opposite end of that
spectrum in which she’s a selfless person

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.169
who wants to serve the greater good.

00:05:32.169 --> 00:05:35.050
At the obvious expense of killing an innocent
girl.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:39.449
So this cold open was actually really important
in the grand scheme of things and shows how

00:05:39.449 --> 00:05:43.130
the TV show medium has an easier time in telling
stories.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.780
Given that they cut to flashbacks without
interrupting the flow of gameplay.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.770
Then the one scene that everyone has been
really excited for is the giraffe scene.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:55.169
This again was a perfect translation from
the game and captures the pure whimsical joy

00:05:55.169 --> 00:05:57.840
that comes from our characters in this moment.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.169
It essentially operates as the calm before
the storm and the pure bliss that the characters

00:06:02.169 --> 00:06:04.080
share here has priceless value.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:09.639
It also acts as a good contrast to the last
episode in which Ellie brutally murders David.

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:13.930
So having this moment kind of brightens up
her mood and she then opens up to Joel.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:17.280
Which I also liked how they made Ellie barely
speak in the beginning.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.240
It was a clever reversal of her character
and it immediately portrays the notion that

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.669
something is wrong with her.

00:06:22.669 --> 00:06:26.889
She’s always been the one to constantly
talk and make jokes and it’s even crazy

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:30.330
how Joel is the one making jokes now considering
his starting point.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:32.560
Along with him opening up more about Sarah.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:36.210
Everything up until this point was basically
pulled from the game, but the addition in

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:40.770
which Joel tried to kill himself adds another
vulnerable layer onto joel that increases

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.110
his overall value in my eyes.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:47.220
The show has really made Joel into a fractured
and hurt individual and the reveal of his

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.280
suicide attempt adds on a brilliant final
layer.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.919
Especially since he lied about it earlier
so the callback here has even more meaning.

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:59.060
Going into one aspect about the episode that
has been getting criticized the most is the

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.060
pacing.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.650
The common complaint is that the episode was
way too fast and they should have slowed down,

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.060
and for once I kind of agree with this sentiment.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:11.770
I do think the pacing was pretty solid and
included no filler at all.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.050
It was very optimal in a way.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:17.590
However, since this is the finale, I think
it should have been longer.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:21.360
Joel and Ellie's current journey into the
city feels kind of weird because it essentially

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.169
has no conflict.

00:07:23.169 --> 00:07:26.919
This is actually the one time where I think
the game did a better job in its execution

00:07:26.919 --> 00:07:28.039
of events.

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:31.780
In the game, they had to maneuver through
a tunnel of infected and eventually they get

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:35.270
to an area that has a rip current going through
one of the tunnels, and Joel and Ellie get

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.410
swept away.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:41.889
When they emerge, Joel is trying to resuscitate
Ellie and in the process, the Fireflies captures

00:07:41.889 --> 00:07:42.889
them.

00:07:42.889 --> 00:07:46.970
To me, this leaves a better ending for Joel
because it acts as more of an emotional cliffhanger

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:47.970
for him.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:51.970
Ellie was on the precipice of death and suddenly
he can’t see her again.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:55.750
It creates a sense of emotional shock for
Joel because the last thing going through

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.409
his mind was Ellie being close to death.

00:07:58.409 --> 00:08:02.759
So the first thing he wants to do upon waking
up is see her again and to reassure his biggest

00:08:02.759 --> 00:08:04.580
worry that she isn’t dead.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.440
This creates more of an urgency to see Ellie
because this is his last memory of her.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.419
Instead of a happy one in which they are sharing
puns.

00:08:12.419 --> 00:08:16.900
Then Marlene denying Joel to see her again
stings that much more because of the way things

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:17.900
ended.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.500
So if they went from the pun scene into a
zombie scene that then gets interrupted by

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.819
the Fireflies, I think it would have flowed
much better.

00:08:24.819 --> 00:08:29.449
Now I don’t think this pacing issue compromises
the climax in the show by any means, but I

00:08:29.449 --> 00:08:32.400
think it is a minor downgrade from the game.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.400
Along with the fact that it would have been
nice to see a bit more zombies.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:39.580
I did just say in my last video that it’s
not a big deal to not include that many zombies

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.769
within this show, but this is the one time
where they would be appropriate.

00:08:43.769 --> 00:08:48.720
It would have given Joel and Ellie one final
obstacle to overcome together before the ending.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.529
Because when you think about it, the last
time they really cooperated was back in episode

00:08:52.529 --> 00:08:53.529
5.

00:08:53.529 --> 00:08:56.589
So seeing them work together as a team to
show their efficiency and growth would have

00:08:56.589 --> 00:08:57.839
been great to see.

00:08:57.839 --> 00:09:01.821
I think this would perfectly tie in the infected
threat and would have easily combated the

00:09:01.821 --> 00:09:04.220
notion of there being a lack of them.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:08.110
There is an infected appearance in the beginning
of the episode, but since Joel and Ellie are

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.320
in a city again, it would make sense to have
an encounter.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:15.160
So while this isn’t a major flaw, I’m
surprised by the rare instance in which the

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.800
game is better than the show for once.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.440
This is a pretty straight adaptation since
there aren’t a lot of original moments here

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:26.170
in the show, and this is a time in which they
should have brought more over from the game.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:30.700
Overall though, I think episode 9 is a slam
dunk in its execution and this marks one of

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:34.550
the best video game to tv show/movie adaptations.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.730
Sitting right next to Arcane in terms of quality.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:40.310
I am really excited to see how they handle
The Last of Us 2.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:44.329
So far they’ve announced that Bella Ramsey
will remain as Ellie which I think is a great

00:09:44.329 --> 00:09:45.329
choice.

00:09:45.329 --> 00:09:48.459
It was kind of in question because of the
second game doing a time jump.

00:09:48.459 --> 00:09:52.740
But she’s 19 so she can definitely play
a slightly more mature version of the character.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.279
Then they’re also going to do 2 seasons
for The Last of Us 2.

00:09:56.279 --> 00:09:59.660
Considering that the game is huge and is like
double the length of the first game.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:03.860
So yeah, thank you for joining me on this
series and I’ll put a playlist of each one

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.439
of my episodic reviews in the end screen.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:10.370
Have a great day and let me know what you
thought about episode 9 of The Last of Us.

